    {
      "id": "uddF1mUnmrKB_8ZjR-6m5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 959.9927840895125,
      "y": 2950.8684512934883,
      "width": 788.9403686523438,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "x3CfU3QXohnr1MRTz_QvY"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1635935675,
      "version": 47,
      "versionNonce": 1402301307,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791390880872,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Controlling sparsity with regularization constraints",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Controlling sparsity with regularization constraints",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "Jl2Q9VRTbjDgF33ebTEwO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 851.5172184970647,
      "y": 3053.3684512934883,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "fUo_oPKRJul2fH1ijuAwI",
        "A9ZvovrNtOzAfKqu8UGCB",
        "YLjtiof-VYYQ55biz2yjh",
        "XhutOtCrnmG61isCrsqNk",
        "0zSaFROMxYQ9K3T6lMzKt",
        "x3CfU3QXohnr1MRTz_QvY"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 840770133,
      "version": 7549,
      "versionNonce": 1801805237,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791390880872,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "To learn which words to keep in the representations, we propose simply adding regularization constraints\non representations when training the model. We use the FLOPS regularizer\n\nSimply speaking, this regularization will penalize words that are often predicted but which are not really\nuseful for retrieving relevant documents. This is useful because, if too many words are added, the lists\nin the inverted index become too big and latency will increase. Using regularization avoids this by\nenabling the model to perform a sort of compression by only retaining the most relevant words from a\ndocument/query.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "To learn which words to keep in the representations, we propose simply adding regularization constraints on representations when training the model. We use the FLOPS regularizer\n\nSimply speaking, this regularization will penalize words that are often predicted but which are not really useful for retrieving relevant documents. This is useful because, if too many words are added, the lists in the inverted index become too big and latency will increase. Using regularization avoids this by enabling the model to perform a sort of compression by only retaining the most relevant words from a document/query.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Qp0siipfnJUNE2xcl7ASC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1163.3473913537132,
      "y": 3513.8939053060412,
      "width": 300.96014404296875,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "3Sw5YReK1wE1VDWXhqelM"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1924609141,
      "version": 20,
      "versionNonce": 188366203,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791390914100,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SPLADE Fine Tuning",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SPLADE Fine Tuning",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "HmZoT40CJ0d8Bdlg7odAY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 865.4384252892601,
      "y": 3634.5939053060415,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "FkoSQXoTgtWOj8R4svBfq",
        "D4LWXpFB0SWYPRA17i-MO",
        "beGSV2IDcPx802ccbHRD9",
        "PV584OzRxW5NihzuVO3sS",
        "efZbnwvkwM6Iekez_vZ6j",
        "L79udJmpJP3V8lg3tTYVS",
        "3Sw5YReK1wE1VDWXhqelM"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1443393557,
      "version": 7585,
      "versionNonce": 179219381,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791390914100,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SPLADE is fine-tuned from a pretrained BERT-base model on a ranking dataset by adapting BERT from\na masked-language-model encoder into a sparse retriever. Instead of predicting a class label, the model\ntakes a query or a document as input and produces a sparse weighted vector over the whole vocabulary.\nThis representation is built from BERT’s contextualized token embeddings and its masked-language-\nmodel head, so the model can assign importance not only to the original input terms but also to useful\nexpansion terms. During fine-tuning, training examples consist of a query, a relevant document, and one\nor more non-relevant documents, including hard negatives and in-batch negatives. The model computes a\nscore for each query-document pair using the dot product between their sparse vectors, and it is\ntrained so that the relevant document receives a higher score than the negatives. At the same time,\nSPLADE applies sparsity regularization to both query and document representations, encouraging most\nvocabulary dimensions to remain zero so retrieval stays efficient. The overall objective therefore\ncombines a ranking loss, which improves relevance, with a regularization term, which controls efficiency. In\nthis way, SPLADE is fine-tuned end-to-end to learn sparse lexical and expansion-aware representations\nthat work effectively for first-stage document retrieval.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SPLADE is fine-tuned from a pretrained BERT-base model on a ranking dataset by adapting BERT from a masked-language-model encoder into a sparse retriever. Instead of predicting a class label, the model takes a query or a document as input and produces a sparse weighted vector over the whole vocabulary. This representation is built from BERT’s contextualized token embeddings and its masked-language-model head, so the model can assign importance not only to the original input terms but also to useful expansion terms. During fine-tuning, training examples consist of a query, a relevant document, and one or more non-relevant documents, including hard negatives and in-batch negatives. The model computes a score for each query-document pair using the dot product between their sparse vectors, and it is trained so that the relevant document receives a higher score than the negatives. At the same time, SPLADE applies sparsity regularization to both query and document representations, encouraging most vocabulary dimensions to remain zero so retrieval stays efficient. The overall objective therefore combines a ranking loss, which improves relevance, with a regularization term, which controls efficiency. In this way, SPLADE is fine-tuned end-to-end to learn sparse lexical and expansion-aware representations that work effectively for first-stage document retrieval.\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
